-### `verify` — check wiki completeness
+### `verify` — check wiki completeness and quality
 
 ```bash
 semanticwiki verify -o ./wiki          # human-readable report
 semanticwiki verify -o ./wiki --json   # JSON output; exit code 1 if incomplete
+semanticwiki verify -r ./my-project -o ./wiki  # include source-reference quality signals
 ```
 
+With `--repo`, the report also checks source-file existence and line ranges,
+scores citation-to-code semantic support with the local BGE embedding model,
+checks required page structure, and parses Mermaid blocks with Mermaid itself.
+During generation,
+`--trajectory ./.semanticwiki/trajectories.jsonl` opt-in captures versioned
+model turns, tool calls/results, and the final quality report for RLVR dataset
+construction. Trajectories may contain source code; keep the file local.
+
